Adaptation_method:
Declare expected arguments explicitly using `.argument()` to handle variable input, or re-enable the previous lenient behavior by calling `.allowExcessArguments(true)`. Example:

Before:
```js
program.option('-p, --port <number>', 'port number');
program.action((options) => {
  console.log(program.args);
});
```

After (recommended):
```js
program.option('-p, --port <number>', 'port number');
program.argument('[args...]', 'remote command and arguments');
program.action((args, options) => {
  console.log(args);
});
```

Or (for backward compatibility):
```js
program.option('-p, --port <number>', 'port number');
program.allowExcessArguments(true);
program.action((options) => {
  console.log(program.args);
});
```
